Subject: [PATCH 303/303] CLAUDE.md -- the 0300 series

The record for 0300-0302, and two entries in the 0200 open list closed
or amended.

The series entry says the thing the three patches have in common, since
it is not what the 0200 series' lesson would have predicted: none of them
was found by a board log. All three are a value that is correct and
published and read by the wrong thing or by nothing, and each needed a
second thing to have happened first -- a file played before a station, a
list with two entries in it, a reader four thousand lines from its
writer. That is the class of fault flashing early does not reach, and it
is worth having beside the 0200 entry that argues for flashing early,
which still stands.

Two rules come out of it and are stated as rules: put a published value
where its reader is rather than where its writer is, because in a single
translation unit the compiler enforces that silently and did so for eight
patches; and adding a mode to a press means finding everything that
describes that press, which is the same shape as the early `continue`
the 0200 series caught three times.

The 0200 entry for the screen is struck through and corrected rather than
just closed. "The screen shows only the station name" was the best case
and not the behaviour, and its guess about why the work was left -- that
it needed ui.c rather than player.c -- was right about the fix and wrong
about the obstacle.

The next/previous entry stays open, with a note that 0302 found part of
why it stayed that way.
